# Test-only helpers that unit tests in other packages import; the tool does not count test code as a caller.
internal/admin/accesstest.RefuseOutsiders # reason: shared by every admin feature's untagged routes_test.go, which deadcode does not analyse
internal/admin/accesstest.RefuseOutsidersOn # reason: the mux half of RefuseOutsiders, called by it and by cmd/goen's untagged route inventory test, which deadcode does not analyse
internal/invoice.Reasons # reason: the closed list of stored reasons, read by the health page's every-reason-has-a-label test and the pin of the stored values; deadcode does not analyse test callers
internal/ui/uitest.AssertEmailLink # reason: shared emailed-link assertion imported by untagged account, newsletter and frame tests and integration handler tests; deadcode excludes those callers
internal/ui/uitest.selectEmailLink # reason: notice-panel selection used only by the shared AssertEmailLink test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.destinationOf # reason: primary action selection used only by the shared emailed-link test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.attr # reason: HTML attribute lookup used only by the shared emailed-link and refusal-summary test assertions; deadcode excludes their test callers
internal/ui/uitest.hasClass # reason: notice-panel and action class matching used only by the shared emailed-link test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.text # reason: heading and reason text extraction used only by the shared emailed-link test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.AssertRefusalSummary # reason: shared page-top refusal assertion imported by the untagged view tests of admin/faq, admin/slides and admin/banners; deadcode excludes those callers
internal/ui/uitest.descendantText # reason: alert and error text extraction used only by the shared refusal-summary test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.refusedPage # reason: indexes the rendered page for the shared refusal-summary test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.summarizes # reason: finds the page-top alert for the shared refusal-summary test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.formBefore # reason: the summary-precedes-forms check of the shared refusal-summary test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.assertInvalidControlsDescribed # reason: the described-controls check of the shared refusal-summary test assertion; deadcode excludes its test callers
internal/ui/uitest.AssertRefusedInput # reason: the refused-input assertion of the back office's integration tests (desks' *_integration_test.go), which deadcode does not analyse; the untagged production build never calls it
internal/ui/uitest.AssertTextNumberControl # reason: the text-number control assertion called only from desks' integration tests, which deadcode does not analyse
internal/ui/uitest.InputAttribute # reason: reads one attribute of an input tag for the desks' integration tests and for AssertRefusedInput and AssertTextNumberControl; deadcode excludes the test callers
internal/ui/uitest.InputElementByID # reason: finds an input tag by id for the desks' integration tests and for AssertRefusedInput and AssertTextNumberControl; deadcode excludes the test callers
internal/ui/uitest.TextareaByID # reason: finds a textarea by id for the desks' integration tests; deadcode excludes those callers
internal/ui/uitest.Browser # reason: the one browser-test skip helper, called only from _browser_test.go files, which deadcode does not analyse
internal/ui/uitest.LocalChrome # reason: the skip helper of the browser test that resolves Chrome itself, called only from a test file, which deadcode does not analyse
internal/ui/uitest.repoRoot # reason: locates scripts/ for LocalChrome, which deadcode reaches only from test files it does not analyse
internal/payment.NewGatewayAt # reason: points a real Gateway at an httptest Stripe stand-in for other packages' untagged and integration tests, which deadcode does not analyse
